1
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:06,140
One can reasonably say that the Montricoux mill has existed since the 8th century.

2
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:12,900
Historically speaking, the Montricoux mill is one of the oldest businesses in the region.

3
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:17,380
And today, it is the last working flour mill in the Tarn-et-Garonne department.

4
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:26,260
Because traditional artisanal bakeries, especially conventional ones, are struggling greatly nowadays, we have to acknowledge that.

5
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:30,060
This is largely due to the rapid expansion of bakery chains.

6
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:34,820
For example, when a bakery chain like Marie Blachère opens in an area,

7
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:39,440
usually two or three independent artisan bakers disappear nearby.

8
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:42,480
That is today’s reality.

9
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:44,140
Fortunately, organic production still exists.

10
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:46,420
These are often very small businesses,

11
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:50,460
but they genuinely support local production and short supply chains,

12
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:51,940
regional wheat varieties, and so on.

13
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:56,800
And they are deeply attached to having a local artisanal mill.

14
00:00:57,780 --> 00:00:59,460
So how do you see the future?

15
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:02,060
I’m not entirely sure yet.

16
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:06,960
The mill building belongs to a family-owned property company.

17
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:08,960
My family.

18
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:13,500
And I operate the business company myself.

19
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:17,600
Previously, it belonged partly to me and partly to my cousin, who was my business partner.

20
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:20,020
Before that, it was my cousin and my father.

21
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:23,040
And before them, my grandfather and an uncle.

22
00:01:23,410 --> 00:01:25,220
It has been a family business for several generations.

23
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:29,520
We are basically the opposite of a startup, if you like.

24
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:33,660
But that does not stop us from creating new things,

25
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:36,280
moving forward, and trying to stay modern.

26
00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:39,280
Though this modernity lies more in ideas and applications

27
00:01:39,870 --> 00:01:40,620
than in the technical process itself.

28
00:01:40,730 --> 00:01:41,920
The technique is ancestral.

29
00:01:42,170 --> 00:01:44,220
A mill’s technique is simply to take wheat,

30
00:01:44,250 --> 00:01:45,600
grind it, and turn it into flour.

31
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:51,680
For example, I am currently working with a researcher who is a nutritionist.

32
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:55,640
The goal is to improve the nutritional value of bread and develop bread recipes

33
00:01:55,860 --> 00:02:00,020
and baking methods that preserve the bread’s nutritional qualities,

34
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:06,360
making it as digestible as possible, including for people intolerant to gluten.

35
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:15,100
Even as a small business, I enjoy developing and creating products,

36
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:18,520
always searching for ways to improve things.